# ─── Elecbits ODM PMS — frontend environment ────────────────────────────────
# Every integration degrades gracefully when unset, so the app runs with zero
# config. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what you want to turn on.
# (`.env` is git-ignored. Only VITE_* vars reach the browser bundle.)

# ── Supabase (cloud database / persistence / login) ─────────────────────────
# Project → Settings → API. With both set, the app (1) requires email/password
# LOGIN via Supabase Auth, (2) loads its user roster from the `profiles` table,
# and (3) persists to Postgres. Run supabase/schema.sql first — it creates every
# table, enables pgvector, and auto-creates a profile on sign-up (the FIRST user
# to register becomes the superadmin). With these unset, the app runs in
# zero-config demo mode: no login, seed users, localStorage.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon public key>

# ── Anthropic (live Claude) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RECOMMENDED: point at the deployed `claude` Edge Function (key stays server-
# side). Its URL looks like the line below.
# VITE_CLAUDE_PROXY_URL=https://<project-ref>.functions.supabase.co/claude
#
# LOCAL DEV ONLY — calls Anthropic directly from the browser and EXPOSES the
# key. Never ship this; use the proxy above instead.
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# Model for all AI calls (default claude-sonnet-4-5).
# VITE_CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5

# ── Google Drive / Sheets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Point at the deployed `drive-sync` Edge Function. The Sync Log then also
# writes to your Google Sheet + Supabase. Empty → Sync Log stays local-only.
# VITE_DRIVE_SYNC_URL=https://<project-ref>.functions.supabase.co/drive-sync
